<title>USA: IFR Systems gets $6.4 mln Army contract.</title>
<headline>IFR Systems gets $6.4 mln Army contract.</headline>
<dateline>WICHITA, Kan. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>IFR Systems Inc said Thursday it was awarded a $6.4 million contract by the U.S. Army to supply software for testing and maintenance of wireless communication systems.</p>
<p>IFR said the contract was for the company's latest version of its AN/GRM-122 test station and related software to the Army during the next 15 months.</p>
<p>((-- Reuter Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
